---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import FilterSim from './FilterSim.astro';
---

<Section id="playground" title="The filter, live.">
  <p class="lede reveal">
    Both of these are blocks I designed for clEAR-ExG, running in your browser
    off their closed-form response. Drag the bias current until the corner lands
    on the dashed line and you have re-derived the number on my resume.
  </p>

  <div class="reveal"><FilterSim /></div>

  <p class="foot reveal">
    Subthreshold model: <code>g<sub>m</sub> = I<sub>D</sub> / nV<sub>T</sub></code>
    with n = 1.5 and V<sub>T</sub> = 25.85 mV. M is the g<sub>m</sub>-division
    ratio real nanopower OTA-C filters use to reach audio-band corners on
    picofarad capacitors. Plots are the exact 2nd-order response; the demo trace
    is filtered by the matching digital biquad.
    <a href="/work/clear-exg">Read how it was actually built →</a>
  </p>
</Section>

<style>
  .lede { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .foot {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--fg-3);
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .foot code { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--fg-2); }
  .foot a { color: var(--accent); border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; }
</style>
